  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "The logic follows here is :\n\n**Square of 3rd term × 3 = 1st term,**\n\n**Square of 3rd term × 2 = 2nd term,**\n\n(243, 162, 9) → (9² × 3 = 243), (9² × 2 = 162)\n\n1). (100, 50, 5) → (5² × 3 ≠ 100), (5² × 2 = 50) \n\n2). (278, 78, 8) → (8² × 3 ≠ 278), (8² × 2 ≠ 78)\n\n**3). (48, 32, 4) → (4² × 3 = 48), (4² × 2 = 32)**\n\n4). (225, 25, 5) → (5² × 3 ≠ 225), (5² × 2 ≠ 25)\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"(48, 32, 4)\".**",
